                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 17:4",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "And there fell ten portions to Manasseh, beside the land of Gilead and Bashan, which were on the other side Jordan;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 85,
            "end": 89
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 17:5",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "Because the daughters of Manasseh had an inheritance among his sons: and the rest of Manasseh’s sons had the land of Gilead.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 17:6",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "And the coast of Manasseh was from Asher to Michmethah, that lieth before Shechem; and the border went along on the right hand unto the inhabitants of En-tappuah.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 13,
            "text": "OR border (also v. 9)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 61,
            "end": 66
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 17:7",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "Now Manasseh had the land of Tappuah: but Tappuah on the border of Manasseh belonged to the children of Ephraim;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 3
          },
          {
            "start": 76,
            "end": 84
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 17:8",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "And the coast descended unto the river Kanah, southward of the river: these cities of Ephraim are among the cities of Manasseh: the coast of Manasseh also was on the north side of the river, and the outgoings of it were at the sea:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 94,
            "end": 97
          },
          {
            "start": 155,
            "end": 158
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 17:9",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "Southward it was Ephraim’s, and northward it was Manasseh’s, and the sea is his border; and they met together in Asher on the north, and in Issachar on the east.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 16
          },
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 48
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 17:10",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "And Manasseh had in Issachar and in Asher Beth-shean and her towns, and Ibleam and her towns, and the inhabitants of Dor and her towns, and the inhabitants of En-dor and her towns, and the inhabitants of Taanach and her towns, and the inhabitants of Megiddo and her towns, even three countries.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 273,
            "end": 277
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 17:11",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "Yet the children of Manasseh could not drive out the inhabitants of those cities; but the Canaanites would dwell in that land.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 67
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 17:12",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "Yet it came to pass, when the children of Israel were waxen strong, that they put the Canaanites to tribute; but did not utterly drive them out.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 100,
            "end": 107,
            "text": "Judg. 1:28."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Judg. 1:28.",
            "prettyString": "Judges 1:28",
            "references": [
